# --- Large binary capture / scan data (multi-GB, regenerable, not source) ---
# Anchored: an unanchored "scan/" also matches engine/scan/, silently hiding
# source files there. The binaries are covered by extension below regardless.
/scan/
gain_ratio_analysis/
*.ARW
*.arw
*.exr
*.tif
*.tiff

# Diagnostic / preview images
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png

# ...except the README gallery, which is a deliverable rather than clutter.
# Every file there is a full-size original, byte-identical to its export and
# carrying its Display P3 profile. Three are HDR and cannot be reduced at all:
# any resize discards the ISO 21496-1 gain map. Sources stay untracked in
# sample_images/.
!docs/samples/*.jpg

# ...and the rendered figure panels, which engine/c41/render_stage_figure.py
# regenerates from a scan that is itself too large to hold here.
!docs/figures/*.jpg

# Staging area for source material: full-size exports, scan EXRs and roll
# anchor JSON. The *published* copies live in docs/samples/ and docs/figures/,
# so nothing here should ever be committed. Ignored wholesale rather than by
# extension, because a 39 MB EXR reaching a public repository is not
# recoverable.
sample_images/

# --- Generated engine outputs ---
out/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- Agent tooling for this working copy, not part of the project ---
# CLAUDE.md, the subagent definitions in .claude/ and the claude.command
# launcher configure how this repository is worked on. They describe a local
# workflow rather than the calibration pipeline, so they stay on disk and out
# of every commit. .claude/worktrees/ is transient in any case.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
claude.command

# Basis-sensitivity ensemble artifacts — reproducible diagnostics, not deliverables
builds/_ensemble/
builds/_forensics/
builds/_corridor/

# Per-camera Status M cubes for the owner's own rigs. Deliberately NOT tracked:
# they are 7.4 MB each, eleven of them, and every refit of the dye sets rewrites
# the whole set, so tracking them grows history by ~81 MB per refit for files
# that are excluded from the release by design (publish-release.sh drops
# ^builds/_). Rebuild them from the canonical dye JSONs whenever a fit changes:
#   c41_statusm_engine.py --stock <k> --sensor <camera> #       --dye-json data/films/<Prefix>_dye_density.json #       --out-cube builds/_a7r3/<Prefix>_StatusM_a7R3.cube
builds/_a7r3/
data/films/_ensemble/

# Per-apparatus cube variants — one named camera each, not deliverables
builds/sensor-*/

# --- Manufacturer datasheets (copyright Kodak / Kodak Alaris / Fujifilm) ---
# Not redistributed. See DATASHEETS.md for how to obtain each sheet; restore
# them to these paths to re-run the digitizers in engine/.
film_datasheet/*.pdf
paper_datasheet/*.pdf
knowledge/Kodak LAD.pdf

# --- Third-party literature (publisher copyright) ---
# Journal articles and conference papers obtained for reference. Never
# redistributed, and never committed in ANY form: the whole directory is
# excluded so that text or image extracts cannot leak past the publish guard.
# That guard now rejects *.pdf, *.txt and any path under literature/, but this
# directory remains the first line of defence. Extract PDFs to a scratch
# directory outside the repository, never in place.
literature/
